<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Links</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
      <h2>HTML Hyperlinks Demonstration</h2>
      <p>Hyperlinks in HTML are created using the <a> tag with the href attribute to specify the link
      destination. The target attribute determines how the link is opened.</p>
      <h2>Basic Hyperlink</h2> 
      <p>Visit the <a href="https://www.google.com./">Google</a> Website. (Open in same Tab.)</p>
      <h2>Open Link in new form</h2>
      <p>If this page is inside a Fram, visite <a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/" target="_blank" >Wikipedia</a> Website. </p>
      <h2>Open Link in Ful window</h2>
      <p>Visite <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news" target="_top">BBC News</a> to load in the full browser window.</p>
      <h2>Open Link in parent Frame</h2>
      <p>If this page is inside a frame, visit <a href="httpa://www.example.com./">example</a> in the parent frame.</p>
  </body>
</html>
